**Algorithm: token bucket via an atomic Lua script (GCRA), not plain INCR+EXPIRE.** Plain `INCR` then `EXPIRE` is two round trips — a race lets a burst slip through right at the boundary, and it doesn't allow controlled burstiness. A single `EVAL`'d Lua script (or a library like `rate-limiter-flexible`'s Redis backend, or the `redis-cell` module) does check-and-increment atomically in one round trip:

```js
